<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeneus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissyl.</span></b> ), ĕi and ĕos,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οινεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a king of
				Ætolia</i> or <i>Calydon</i>, <i>the husband of Althœa</i>, <i>and father of Meleager</i>, <i>Tydeus</i>, <i>Dejanira</i>, <i>Gorgo</i>, etc., <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 281 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				172</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 2, 165</span></i>; <i><span class="en">586</span></i>;
			Cic. poët. Tusc. 2, 8, 20.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oenēis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἰνηΐς</span>, <i>the daughter
				of Œneus</i>, i. e. <i>Dejanira</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Sen. Herc. Oet.
			583</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oenēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἰνήϊος</span>, <i>Œnean</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oeneius heros,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Tydeus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 5, 661</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oenēus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), a,
			um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἰνήϊος</span>, <i>Œnean</i>: Oeneos
			per agros, i. e. <i>of Calydon</i> or <i>Ætolia</i>, Ov M. 8, 281.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Oenīdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οἰνείδης</span>, <i>a male descendant of
				Œneus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">at manus Oenidae variat,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Meleager</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					8, 414</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 3, 690</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et generum Oeniden, Appule Daune, tuum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Diomedes</i>, <i>son of Tydeus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					4, 76</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. M. 14, 512</span></i>.</div>
